# KLM791.json

Dataset: avia-flights — Airborne times of 127 long-haul routes, both directions, with filed flight
  plans (FlightAware)
File: data/avia/flights/raw/KLM791.json
SHA-256: 5ca6e980738ec7616062d01726232ec50af7b3ca3c4a22cd8c20c58a72de4041 (also in
  data/avia/flights/inputs.lock; check with: cd data/avia/flights && sha256sum -c inputs.lock)
In the public repository: no, only this description and the hash: FlightAware's terms of use do not
  allow republishing what is read from its pages. Get it from fog fetch avia-flights, then compare
  its SHA-256 with the one above.
Obtained: values extracted from web pages.
From: FlightAware public flight pages of each callsign, read 2026-09-28, 2026-11-06 and 2026-11-25
  (fog fetch avia-flights): wheels-off and wheels-on times, filed flight plan, airport coordinates.
Fetching it again: not possible: FlightAware shows a flight's history for a limited time, so
  fetching again gives other flights, on other days. The values used (wheels-off and wheels-on
  times, filed routes and speeds, airports) are in src/data/presets/avia-flights.js, generated from
  these files, with this file's hash in its header.
Checks: Flights without both times or with a diversion are dropped and counted by the build.
What could still be wrong: FlightAware's times come from ADS-B and airline messages; a mislabelled
  leg or a wrong time zone on their page would pass through.
Collected: 2026-11-25
Licence: other — FlightAware public flight pages (https://www.flightaware.com), read 2026-09-28,
  2026-11-06 and 2026-11-25 (three windows of about two weeks, kept together); check FlightAware's
  terms of use before re-fetching on a large scale.
Sources:
- FlightAware, public flight pages (actual wheels-off / wheels-on times, filed flight plans, airport
  reference coordinates) <https://www.flightaware.com>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- plan.nm: planned distance filed by the airline, computed on the WGS84 ellipsoid (stored, not used
  for the radius)
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): Southern round trips that take about twice as long as
  equally long northern ones, as the flat map's distances require; or times that fit the flat map's
  distances better than the globe's.
Built by: fog build avia-flights, fog build avia-mesh
Generated files:
- src/data/presets/avia-flights.js
- src/data/presets/avia-mesh.js
Code:
- tools/internal/build/aviaflights
- tools/internal/build/aviamesh
- src/tabs/avia/values.js
- src/tabs/avia/radius.js
- src/tabs/avia/meshfig.js
Shown on the page:
- #tab-avia/avia-h2g
- #tab-avia/avia-h2rf
- #tab-avia/avia-h2m
Notes: Edit routes.json only (one entry per airport pair, ICAO callsigns each way), then fog fetch
  avia-flights, fog lock avia-flights, fog build avia-flights. The times, the airports' coordinates
  (angles), the waypoints and the filed true airspeed (a speed through the air, from Mach and
  temperature, not over the ground) carry no radius: the radius of the avia tab uses only those, so
  it is a measure. The filed distances do carry one and are flagged above, which is why the dataset
  as a whole is a check.

Written by `fog build explain` from data/avia/flights/dataset.json and data/avia/flights/inputs.lock: edit those, not this file.
